  "body": "Asked by mkinney (2026-11-18): \"If we get confused by those terms, then so will users/others. Make sure it is clear in the docs.\"\n\nTwo different things are both called \"mill-turn\":\n- **Live tooling / lathe milling:** a lathe (multitasking turning centre) that also mills with driven tools, often with a C axis and sometimes a Y axis. This is CamCraft's built-in \"Mill-turn\" machine (loads as \"MULTITASKING 5-AXIS\").\n- **Turning on a mill (part in spindle):** a 3-axis mill used as a lathe - the part turns in the mill spindle, lathe tools sit on the table, one work offset per tool (Tormach RapidTurn style). Not supported yet (#2580).\n\nWhat to change:\n- A short glossary box with both terms in the turning guide (`site/content/guide/operations/operations-turning.md`), the machine documentation, and the `camcraft-mcp` skill's machine list.\n- Never use a bare \"mill-turn\" in docs or UI text without saying which one; the ribbon's MILL-TURNING tab names the live-tooling kind.\n\nDone means: the glossary is in those three places, and a search of the docs for \"mill-turn\" finds no use that leaves the meaning open.\n",
